// What a file name cannot say.
//
// Every picture in this tree declares itself: `interface/icons/icon_diplomacy.svg` is the
// sprite `icon_diplomacy` because that is what it is called. A mod replaces it by putting
// a file of the same name anywhere in its own gfx/ tree, and writes nothing here at all.
//
// This file is for the rest: how many frames a strip holds, a tint to multiply a picture
// by, or a sprite whose name should differ from its file. Paths, when given, are relative
// to gfx/ - so the same line means the same thing in the base game and in a mod.
{
  "sprites": {
    // Four arrowheads across one sheet: move, prepared attack, live attack, fall back.
    "globe_plan_arrows": { "frames": 4 }
  }
}
